# HITL morning checklist sync

The Human-in-the-Loop morning checklist lives on GitLab `cursor-test` at:

`admin-guide/Cursor-Docs-as-Code.md` → **§2. Human-in-the-Loop (HITL) morning checklist**

Whenever you make an **operational** change that affects how morning checks are done, **update that table in the same task** (Where to look, Look for, Success, and Action on failure columns as needed). Add or remove rows when a check is introduced or retired. Trim stale cells; do not only append contradictory instructions.

When `cursor-test` is in the workspace, prefer editing that file directly. If it is not open, say that the HITL table still needs updating on `cursor-test` before claiming the ops change is done.

## What counts as operational

Update the HITL table when you change any of these surfaces (or their operator docs / schedules / entry points):

| HITL check (row) | Typical paths / systems |
| :--- | :--- |
| GitLab plugin MRs | GitLab MR workflow, Assignee policy, Bugbot/Approval review process for `cursor-test` |
| Michu overnight run | `michu/`, Michu automation prompt/schedule/webhook, `upstream_doc_snapshot`, `doc-drift` MR conventions |
| Trundle overnight run | `trundle/`, Trundle automation prompt/schedule, hygiene report paths, changelog `### Summary` ownership |
| Vulnerability Scanner / Security Agents | Security Agents dashboard binding, triage policy in `Cursor-Security.md` / Docs-as-Code §7.6 |
| Inbox CI / automation mail | Notification expectations tied to GitLab/ADO CI or Automations (when you document them) |
| GitLab CI on `main` | `.gitlab-ci.yml` jobs operators must watch (`docs_lint`, `mirror_to_ado`, schedules) |
| `vendor_doc_links` | Trundle vendor schedule, `trundle/vendor-doc-links.yaml`, artifact path under `trundle/reports/vendor-link-check/` |
| Changelog health | Changelog Summary/Changes layout, `sync_id` backfill behaviour |
| Automations still enabled | Michu/Trundle Automations UI settings (Run as, model, schedule) documented for operators |
| ParaDOCS / Paragon Knowledge (optional) | Local plugin install / MCP Connected troubleshooting that operators check daily |
| Admin Dashboard glance (optional) | Admin Dashboard runbook entry points used in the morning glance |

## Required behaviour

1. After an operational edit, open §2 of `Cursor-Docs-as-Code.md` and check whether any row is now wrong, incomplete, or missing.
2. Update the matching row(s) surgically (ADO wiki HTML table). Keep bullet lists in Where to look / Look for / Success / Action on failure.
3. Keep first Michu / Trundle mentions linked to their Docs-as-Code H2s (`#11-…`, `#12-…`) and other Where-to-look links accurate.
4. Route a changelog row on `cursor-test` (`Docs-as-code workflow`) when the HITL table itself changes.
5. Distinguish from §13 Verification checklist (post-merge publish checks). Do not merge those two tables.

## Do not

- Skip the HITL update because the primary edit was in `michu/`, `trundle/`, CI, or Security docs only.
- Duplicate the whole checklist into the plugin repo; `cursor-test` remains canonical.
- Rewrite the table for tone-only or style-only guide edits that do not change operator morning behaviour.
- Edit the ADO mirror for the table; edit GitLab `cursor-test` only.
